  characterName: Ama Koranteng
  promptText: An export firm offers a long-term cocoa contract that replaces mixed
    forest with monoculture, promising steady income and guaranteed buyers. Signing
    secures cash but reduces river flow, wild foods and community resilience.
  leftAnswer: A reliable contract could stabilise household income and market access.
  rightAnswer: Keeping the mixed forest preserves water, food sources and long-term
    resilience.
